From f43ddbb3ce82236406e96ff520f3f1b0c20be8af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: codEx Fork Bot <codex-fork-bot@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:32:05 +0800
Subject: rewind: scope snapshot chains per conversation

- Each conversation (thread) now owns an independent snapshot chain under
  threads/<conversation-id>/, following Claude Code's per-session
  checkpoint model. Conversations never evict each other's snapshots, and
  snapshot numbering matches the transcript ordinals the pickers use, so
  the cross-conversation prompt-matching fallback is no longer needed for
  ordinary cases.
- The Files-only picker aggregates the legacy chain and every conversation
  chain, labeling each snapshot with a short conversation id.
- Conversation rewinds resolve and restore inside the current thread's
  chain; the legacy workspace-wide chain remains supported for snapshots
  created before per-conversation chains existed.
- Pruning is per chain and garbage collection unions references across all
  chains; adds regression tests for per-conversation isolation,
  independent pruning, and thread-scoped restore.
